## 🔴 CRITICAL — blocks "perfect" documentation

Items in this section, if unfilled, prevent the documentation from reaching the agreed quality threshold. The CIDRA framework will explicitly note these gaps in every output file's Limitations section.

```
☐  1. [item name]
       Why critical: [explanation]
       Without this we cannot: [specific limitation]

☐  2. ...
```

---

## 🟡 HIGH — significantly improves quality

```
☐  N. [item name]
       Why high-value: [explanation]
       With this we could additionally: [enhancement]
```

---

## 🟢 MEDIUM — adds context

```
☐  N. [item name]
       Adds: [context/color]
```

---

## ✗ Acknowledged gaps (customer declined to provide)

Items the customer explicitly confirmed will NOT be provided. Documentation proceeds with these gaps recorded as risk:

```
✗  N. [item name]
       Customer reason: "..."
       Documentation note: explicit Limitations section entry
```

---

## How to respond

For each unchecked item above:
- **✓** = "I'll provide it"
- **✗** = "We can't / won't provide it" (acknowledged risk)
- **?** = "Need to investigate — checking with team"

Return this file with marks. Items left unmarked are treated as **?** and re-surfaced at the next checkpoint.

